  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run: 8 witnesses, 19 names, no composed rules. That used 1 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_497.lean`)\n- **Who it applies to:** the subject is a vehicle (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`) on a one-way roadway. That roadway lies on a highway, and some lane lies on the same highway.\n- **What it forbids:** for every such roadway (selected again exactly as above), the car may not be all three of these at once:\n  - parked, using `drv_motion_parked` with the two reading parameters;\n  - on the roadway's left-hand side. That means the road edge nearest the car (smallest absolute lateral offset) is on its left relative to the roadway's direction. I wrote this as \"the edge's offset times (car heading · roadway direction) is positive\". This covers the record's two cases and works whichever way the car faces.\n  - not covered by any permitting device. That means no parking bay under the car, and no angle-parking sign or parking-restricted zone sign that applies to it and governs a road area it occupies.\n- I declared no narrowings. Ties for \"nearest edge\" are written as \"no farther than every other edge\"; this only matters if two edges are exactly equally near.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_497.lean`)\n- The setting is a two-lane eastbound one-way roadway with a curb on each side. The car sits 1.5 m from the left curb and 5.5 m from the right one, or the reverse in `permit`.\n- All six planned scenarios are built. I added `branch_3` (angle-parking sign) and `branch_4` (parking-restricted zone sign) so both sign cases are tested.\n- Each witness is judged only from 70 s on, so the 60 s look-back for \"parked\" stays inside the recording.\n\nBefore the first gate run, I tried the gate command with `--help` added. The permission layer blocked it: the session allows only the exact gate command. It didn't run and didn't use a gate run.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
